From 298452458b04cbe5a725ed1083201b1f25fcce8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JakeStone <208141191+JakeStone594@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:59:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: f_hid: move list and spinlock inits from bind to
 alloc
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Backport of upstream "usb: gadget: f_hid: move list and spinlock inits
from bind to alloc" (Michael Zimmermann, 2026-03-31). CVE-2026-31721,
CVSS 3.1 5.5 AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H — availability only,
a local DoS, NOT privilege escalation as some vendor advisories title it.

hidg_bind() re-initialised state that belongs to the lifetime of the
gadget function, not of a bind: two spinlocks, two wait queue heads and
one list head. init_waitqueue_head() resets the head's task_list to
self-pointing, so a poll/select waiter registered before a UDC unbind
is silently orphaned across the rebind; its poll_freewait() ->
remove_wait_queue() -> list_del() then walks a head that no longer
references the entry.

Reproduced on this device on v6 (2026-08-23): 3x "list_del corruption"
via __list_del_entry_valid+0xa8 <- remove_wait_queue+0x28 <-
poll_freewait+0x38 <- do_select. Non-fatal only because commit 7b96ece4a
keeps the struct alive, so the walk hits valid memory and
__list_del_entry_valid declines the delete. On v5 the same walk hit
freed slab and reset the phone.

Note CONFIG_DEBUG_LIST=y is the only reason this is observable here:
SLUB_DEBUG and DEBUG_OBJECTS are both unset. Taint cannot detect it —
bit 9 (W) is already set by a boot-time rcu WARN, so any taint-keyed
health check is blind to every WARN after the first of a boot.

Scope differs from upstream, and the difference is real rather than a
judgement call: upstream moves nine initialisations, of which four
concern members 4.14.190 does not have (get_report_spinlock, get_queue,
get_id_queue, report_list — grep count 0 each). The five that exist are
moved. write_pending and req stay in bind; they are genuinely per-bind,
exactly as upstream leaves them.

Beyond upstream, deliberately: the two per-bind stores are now taken
under write_spinlock. Today they are unlocked stores to lock-protected
fields, which is masked because the lock is re-initialised immediately
above them. Once the lock becomes persistent that mask is gone and the
race is real: a writer blocked in f_hidg_write()'s WRITE_COND loop on an
fd that survived unbind — which 7b96ece4a deliberately makes possible —
can take the lock, pass the check, and read hidg->req while bind stores
NULL to it outside the lock. The re-check at the copy_from_user() site
comes after the dereference.

Verified: unpatched control object built first in an isolated out dir,
its .text byte-identical to the shipped v6 f_hid.o (3f1bbd83...), so the
build environment reproduces the running kernel; patched .text then
differs (d04c6f0f...); compiles rc=0 with zero warnings; both
__init_waitqueue_head relocations move out of hidg_bind into hidg_alloc.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013ydNrFirMZjskYMZST87ez
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c | 14 +++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c
index 5d73d6ed0..f544d1d8d 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c
@@ -758,6 +758,7 @@ static int hidg_bind(struct usb_configuration *c, struct usb_function *f)
 	struct usb_ep		*ep;
 	struct f_hidg		*hidg = func_to_hidg(f);
 	struct usb_string	*us;
+	unsigned long		flags;
 	int			status;
 
 	/* maybe allocate device-global string IDs, and patch descriptors */
@@ -822,13 +823,10 @@ static int hidg_bind(struct usb_configuration *c, struct usb_function *f)
 	if (status)
 		goto fail;
 
-	spin_lock_init(&hidg->write_spinlock);
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&hidg->write_spinlock, flags);
 	hidg->write_pending = 1;
 	hidg->req = NULL;
-	spin_lock_init(&hidg->read_spinlock);
-	init_waitqueue_head(&hidg->write_queue);
-	init_waitqueue_head(&hidg->read_queue);
-	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&hidg->completed_out_req);
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&hidg->write_spinlock, flags);
 
 	/* create char device */
 	cdev_init(&hidg->cdev, &f_hidg_fops);
@@ -1091,6 +1089,12 @@ static struct usb_function *hidg_alloc(struct usb_function_instance *fi)
 	if (!hidg)
 		return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
 
+	spin_lock_init(&hidg->write_spinlock);
+	spin_lock_init(&hidg->read_spinlock);
+	init_waitqueue_head(&hidg->write_queue);
+	init_waitqueue_head(&hidg->read_queue);
+	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&hidg->completed_out_req);
+
 	opts = container_of(fi, struct f_hid_opts, func_inst);
 
 	mutex_lock(&opts->lock);
